IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `expl-rules`

-- Explosives Act 1961 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `Part II applies` (`Explosives case` OF `the Commonwealth's, or in its possession or control`, FALSE, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT `Part II applies` (`Explosives case` OF `made by the Commonwealth and being exported under an arrangement with it`, FALSE, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT `Part II applies` (`Explosives case` OF `a foreign government's or forces', here with Commonwealth approval for defence`, FALSE, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Part II applies` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, FALSE, 0, FALSE))
#ASSERT `the maximum months for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, TRUE, 0, FALSE) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, TRUE, 0, FALSE) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, TRUE, 5, FALSE) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, FALSE, 5, FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the explosives position for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, TRUE, 0, TRUE))'s `a lesser prescribed penalty applies instead`
#ASSERT `the maximum months for` (`Explosives case` OF `anyone else's`, TRUE, 0, TRUE) EQUALS 0
